    "done_when": "tests/test_crew_record_liveness.py::test_no_module_decides_record_liveness_with_a_bare_pid passes. The defect, named by run r-20261001T201141795077: reckon/crew/recovery.py:4638 _worker_record_liveness probes the worker record's pid with the bare runs.process_alive and re-implements the start-time comparison that runs.record_process_alive owns, and classify_pointer reaches it without the host gate (recovery.py:5539, feeding superseded_manifest at 5716-5723), so a foreign run whose worker-record pid happens to be live here can have its terminal manifest deferred as superseded. A new tests/test_a_foreign_worker_record_does_not_defer_a_manifest.py drives that foreign case and asserts the terminal manifest is honoured. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of tests/test_crew_record_liveness.py, tests/test_a_live_run_never_reads_dead.py and tests/test_a_resume_does_not_inherit_its_baseline.py show zero added failures.",
